ss  from the right angle okay that's 5 so  the sine ratio is going to be 3/5 if we  want to find the cosecant okay this is  abbreviated as CSC the cosecant we can  just take the reciprocal that's going to  be 5 over 3 another way to think about  this though is instead of the opposite  over hypotenuse you can do the  hypotenuse over the opposite okay the  next one the cosine of theta we're going  to use the adjacent over hypotenuse so  if we're here adjacent means next to  that's going to be this side here that's  4  over the hypotenuse which is five so  that's four-fifths for the cosine now  students sometimes make a mistake they  say well Mario you know isn't five  adjacent to two the angle theta well  that is true adjacent means next to but  the one that's across from the right  angle we're always gonna call that the  hypotenuse so the adjacent side is the  other one that's next to it okay and  then the secant of theta that's the  reciprocal of cosine so seeking is  abbreviated SEC and you can just take  the reciprocal or flip that fraction  over so five over four and then the last  one the tangent of theta we're using the  opposite over the adjacent so tangent we  have opposite that's a cross adjacent  that's next to the angle so that's gonna  be three over four and then the  cotangent we're just gonna take the  reciprocal so that's 4/3  okay so let's jump into some other  examples so you can get some experience  with this so number one we want to find  the six trigonometric functions okay of  this angle here okay so if you're here  at this angle you can see we're missing  this side right here so we have to do  the Pythagorean theorem to find this  missing side so this is a right triangle  here so we've got a squared plus B  squared equals C squared right seven is  going to be our a B squared we don't  know that's the side right here and C  squared is our hypotenuse that's  twenty-five squared this is 625 7  squared is 49 if we subtract 49 from  both sides what do we get we get 576 and  if we take the square root we get 24 so  this is 24 now you might know this  already if you learned your Pythagorean  triples these are integer values so  these are ones that are easy to work  with this one here is gonna be a little  bit more challenging we're to have some  radicals so but for this one now we've  got all three sides let's say we want to  find the sine of theta so sine of theta  equals opposite side over the hypotenuse  right so opposite would be 7 hypotenuse  is across from the right angle so that's  going to be 25 and you've got it if we  want the cosecant of theta we just take  the reciprocal this is going to be 25  over 7 okay how about the cosine of  theta well cosine is adjacent over  hypotenuse so see a over H so adjacent  is next 2 that's 24 over the one across  from the right angle that is the  hypotenuse so 24 over 25 if we want the  secant  sec we just take the reciprocal this is  going to be 25 over 24 and then if we  want the tangent tangent is opposite  divided by the adjacent remember  opposites across that's seven and  adjacent is next to so that's going to  be seven over 24 and if you want the  cotangent Co T of the angle we're just  going to take the reciprocal that's 24 /  7
 

